@startuml
title UC8 - Matchmaking - Test Cases

map "TC-UC8-01: Successful matchmaking" as TC1 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC8-01
  Test Case Name => Successfully find PvP opponent
  Description => Verify Champion player can find an opponent through matchmaking
  Preconditions => 1. Player is logged in with Champion status \n 2. Network connection available \n 3. Another player is in queue
  Test Case Input => Player: "player1" (Champion) \n Server: PvP Server online
  Expected Output => 1. Connected to PvP Server via SignalR \n 2. Placed in matchmaking queue \n 3. Opponent found \n 4. BattleRoom created \n 5. Transition to UC9
  Steps => 1. Select PvP Battle from Main Menu \n 2. System verifies Champion status \n 3. System connects to PvP Server \n 4. System sends matchmaking request \n 5. Server finds opponent \n 6. Verify match notification \n 7. Verify transition to PvP Battle
  Default Value Preserving => No data changes until battle begins
}

map "TC-UC8-02: Matchmaking blocked - not Champion" as TC2 {
  Test Case Number => TC-UC8-02
  Test Case Name => Matchmaking rejected for non-Champion player
  Description => Verify non-Champion player cannot access PvP matchmaking
  Preconditions => 1. Player is logged in \n 2. Player has NOT completed Pokemon League (IsChampion = false)
  Test Case Input => Player: "newplayer" (IsChampion = false)
  Expected Output => 1. System displays requirement message \n 2. Player returns to Main Menu \n 3. No server connection attempted
  Steps => 1. Select PvP Battle from Main Menu \n 2. System checks Champion status \n 3. System finds IsChampion = false \n 4. Verify requirement message displayed \n 5. Verify return to Main Menu \n 6. Verify no network call made
  Default Value Preserving => No changes to player data or server state
}

@enduml
